cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "tei-line-ends: OCR correction at the line break in TEI"
message: "If you use these tools, please cite them."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lendl
    given-names: Christian
repository-code: "https://github.com/USER/tei-line-ends"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-12
keywords:
  - TEI
  - OCR post-correction
  - Transkribus
  - digital humanities
abstract: >-
  Two chains of tools that correct OCR errors at the line break in TEI
  transcriptions: line-break hyphenation (is a break a real hyphen, or an
  artefact of the line?) and misread line-final characters (Wien transcribed
  as Wier). Both build their reference lexicon from the corpus itself, from
  line-interior tokens that a line break cannot have damaged, and both keep
  every machine proposal in a ranked CSV decision store that a human outranks,
  so no detector ever writes to the transcription.
